  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.32\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.32 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.31\n- First published release of this package.\n- Adds DeviceCheck and App Attest attestation providers for iOS, macOS, and Mac Catalyst, plus `AppAttestWithDeviceCheckFallback`.\n- App Attest registration state is scoped by Firebase App ID: the key identifier is stored in user defaults and the artifact in the Keychain. Fallback selects DeviceCheck only when App Attest is unsupported; an App Attest operation failure does not trigger fallback.\n- Adds the `X-Ios-Bundle-Identifier` header to App Check calls.\n- Options: `Provider`, `KeychainAccessGroup`, and `AttestationTimeout` (60 seconds by default).\n- Multi-targets `net10.0-ios`, `net10.0-macos`, and `net10.0-maccatalyst` with no MAUI dependency and no third-party Firebase bindings. Minimum OS versions: iOS 15.0, macOS 10.15, Mac Catalyst 15.0.\n- Enable the App Attest capability in your entitlements when using `AppAttest` or `AppAttestWithDeviceCheckFallback`, and set `KeychainAccessGroup` only when the matching Keychain Sharing entitlement exists. The package adds no manifest or entitlement entries.",
